FinTrust — vendored, modified
=============================

Upstream
    FinTrust: A Comprehensive Benchmark of Trustworthiness Evaluation in Finance
    Domain. Hu, Hu, Bai, Zhao, Cohan and Zhao. Proceedings of the 2025
    Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP 2025),
    pages 10099-10128. arXiv:2510.15232
    Dataset: https://huggingface.co/datasets/HughieHu/FinTrust

    Upstream ships no LICENSE file. This copy is redistributed for the sole
    purpose of reproducing the evaluation reported in the accompanying paper.
    Contact the upstream authors for licensing terms.

What this benchmark is used for here
    The fourteen-metric compliance audit across seven dimensions reported in
    paper section 5.4 — trustfulness, robustness, safety, fairness, privacy,
    transparency and knowledge discovery.

Modifications made to the upstream release
    config/config.yaml, inference.py, evaluation.py
        Added. Upstream runs each dimension through its own api_call.py and
        postprocess_response.py by hand. These wrap all seven dimensions behind
        the same config.yaml + inference.py + evaluation.py interface used by
        the other two vendored harnesses, driving them against a locally served
        vLLM checkpoint.
    api_utils.py, retry_errors.py, summarize_results.py
        Added. Shared client, retry handling for partial dimension failures, and
        a single summary across all fourteen metrics.
    <dimension>/api_call.py, <dimension>/postprocess_response.py
        Modified across every dimension to route through api_utils.py rather
        than each holding its own client and credentials.

Note on generated files
    FinTrust writes each model's responses into the same directory as the
    dataset that produced them. Generated files carry an `output` segment in
    their name and are excluded by .gitignore; the twelve
    `<task>_evaluation_<N>.json{,l}` input datasets are tracked.
